{"content":"---\nname: project-shadow-frontier\ndescription: \"Shadow Frontier: successor project to the defect-cocycle program — narrow-band exclusion proved+certified, run-budget clock, exact (D,eps) phase diagram with two arithmetic lines\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 3d506146-0c9f-463a-a710-cacb38cea0a3\n---\n\n**Shadow Frontier** at `/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/` (syracuse-confinement repo). Successor to [[project-defect-cocycle-csuite]] per `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/critiques/dc_next_steps.md`. Targets: (1) banded S-unit rigidity, (2) band-crossing certificate, (3) mixed-tower enumeration.\n\n**Proved / certified (as of 2026-06-10):**\n- **Narrow-band dichotomy** (`notes/narrowband.tex`, 4pp): divergent orbits dwell ≤ O(Y^θ(D)) in bands of ratio < 2^{2D*}; full exclusion (incl. cycles, via Baker τ=13.3) at ratio ≲2.1; bounded-discrepancy exclusion complexity-free.\n- **Exact count method** (`search/exact_count.py`, `search/vhires_phase.c`): D-confinement quantizes B_j to ≤⌊2D⌋+1 integers around j·log₂3 ⟹ N_D(p) by rotation-driven bigint recursion, NO discretization. **D\\* = 1.246, band ratio 5.63** (supersedes δ-grid 1.232/5.5); theorem hypothesis uses exact integer N_D(p), Perron eliminated.\n- **Run-budget/ghost-depth clock** (`notes/runbudget.tex`): maximal b=1 run length = v₂(x+1)−1 EXACTLY, depth −1/step (S(x)+1 = 3(x+1)/2); Target 2 = single renewal coordinate \"no orbit oversamples its own ghost depths forever\". Measured: global depth law = natural 2^{−(g−1)}; ascending windows oversample (mean 3.68 vs 3.01).\n- **Exact (D,ε) phase diagram** (2000×1500×24ω×400t, C/OpenMP ~90s/24 cores, `viz/fig5_phase_diagram_vhires.png`): two arithmetic lines — vertical D\\*=1.246 (counting capacity) and horizontal **binary bias ceiling ε_bin = √(9/196+3(log₂3−19/14)²) = 0.44903** (alphabet capacity: calibrated {1,2}-words can't exceed it; crossing needs b≥3 letters taxed by run-budget clock). Boundary kinks at 2D∈ℤ (window-size jumps) are real; δ-grid scallops were artifacts (|Δθ| median 0.02, max 0.53). ε\\* saturates ≈0.54.\n\n**Pilot 001:** 120/120 calibrated biased high-complexity candidates = ghosts. Ghost catalog in `catalog/ghost_catalog.tex` (incl. −5, −17 cycle calcs).\n\n**Open next:** depth-oversampling lemma → Target-2 theorem; interval-certified λ(D,ε) boundary (mechanical now via exact engine); dip-tolerant crossing windows at scale; S-unit exponent-vector rank diagnostic (Target 1).\n","filePath":"/home/john/.claude/projects/-home-john-mynotes/memory/project_shadow_frontier.md","originalFile":"---\nname: project-shadow-frontier\ndescription: \"Shadow Frontier: successor project to the defect-cocycle program — S-unit rigidity, band-crossing certificates, high-complexity trap search\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 3d506146-0c9f-463a-a710-cacb38cea0a3\n---\n\n**Shadow Frontier** at `/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/` (in the syracuse-confinement repo; pushed 2026-06-10, commit 9a74c80). Successor to [[project-defect-cocycle-csuite]] per `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/critiques/dc_next_steps.md`.\n\n**Mission:** the surviving Collatz counterexample class after the Finite Spectral Shadows program = high-complexity, calibrated (mean → log₂3), non-coboundary phase-biased, mixed-(2,3)-adically coherent ghost resisting every finite max-plus certificate. Three targets:\n1. **Banded S-unit rigidity** (Target 1): many block identities 2^B x′ − 3^p x = A in a band ⟹ exponent vectors (B_{i,j}, p−1−j) collapse to finitely many linear patterns (ESS/subspace) = repeated/periodic blocks = dead. Diagnostic: Z-rank of exponent-vector differences in high-deviation vs ordinary windows.\n2. **Band-crossing certificate** (Target 2): no-long-banded-windows escape ⟹ fast band crossing ⟹ b=1-density > ½+δ ⟹ 2-adic near-ghost (x ≡ −1 mod 2^{f(δ)m}) vs positivity. Quantify the all-ones exclusion.\n3. **Mixed-tower certificate enumeration** (Target 3): Karp max-plus over 2^a3^b for symbolic candidates.\n\n**Tooling:** `search/frontier.py` — candidate gen (letter law {1,2,4} with mean=log₂3 + prescribed ord-3 bias), calibration, complexity, 2-adic realizability (ghost test from the predecessor's sturmian_ghost machinery), mixed-tower traps + Karp, expvec rank.\n\n**Pilot 001:** 120/120 calibrated biased high-complexity candidates = ghosts (full-bit-length least reps, no stabilization); none positive-realizable. Q3 (PROGRAM.md): entropy-vs-bias tension — max-entropy law subject to biased marginal is Markov; does its complexity meet the repetition-rigidity threshold in windows?\n\nAIPM initialized (ailog validate ✓). Final dichotomy: long banded windows ⟹ S-unit rigidity; none ⟹ band-crossing certificate.\n","structuredPatch":[{"lines":[" ---"," name: project-shadow-frontier","-description: \"Shadow Frontier: successor project to the defect-cocycle program — S-unit rigidity, band-crossing certificates, high-complexity trap search\"","+description: \"Shadow Frontier: successor project to the defect-cocycle program — narrow-band exclusion proved+certified, run-budget clock, exact (D,eps) phase diagram with two arithmetic lines\""," metadata: ","   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: 3d506146-0c9f-463a-a710-cacb38cea0a3"," ---"," ","-**Shadow Frontier** at `/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/` (in the syracuse-confinement repo; pushed 2026-06-10, commit 9a74c80). Successor to [[project-defect-cocycle-csuite]] per `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/critiques/dc_next_steps.md`.","+**Shadow Frontier** at `/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/` (syracuse-confinement repo). Successor to [[project-defect-cocycle-csuite]] per `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/critiques/dc_next_steps.md`. Targets: (1) banded S-unit rigidity, (2) band-crossing certificate, (3) mixed-tower enumeration."," ","-**Mission:** the surviving Collatz counterexample class after the Finite Spectral Shado